,{"n":"Farmácia Moderna de Matosinhos","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":41.180552,"lo":-8.689753,"d":899},{"n":"Santander","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":41.180209,"lo":-8.689778,"d":909,"h":"Mo-Fr 08:30-15:00; Sa-Su off; Jan 01,Apr 25,May 25,Jun 01,Jun 26,Aug 10,Aug 24,Oct 15,Nov 05,Dec 01,Dec 08,Dec 25 off","w":"https://www.santander.pt/","wifi":1},{"n":"LIGATU","g":"essentials","k":"mobile_phone","la":41.181923,"lo":-8.689079,"d":921},{"n":"Tidal pools of Leça de Palmeira","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.192778,"lo":-8.707778,"d":1267,"ds":"The Tidal Pools of Leça da Palmeira (Portuguese: Piscina das Marés de Leça da Palmeira) is a public swimming pool on the beach of Leça da Palmeira in Matosinhos municipality, in the district of Porto, Portugal. The structures consist of two natural pools filled with fresh sea water, designed and built between 1960 and 1973 by Portuguese architect Álvaro Siza Vieira.","wpu":"Tidal pools of Leça de Palmeira","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Swimmingpool_on_the_Beach_at_Le%C3%A7a_da_Palmeira_by_Christian_G%C3%A4nshirt.JPG/960px-Swimmingpool_on_the_Beach_at_Le%C3%A7a_da_Palmeira_by_Christian_G%C3%A4nshirt.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sea Life Porto","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.168056,"lo":-8.687222,"d":1976,"ds":"Sea Life Porto is an aquarium located in Porto, Portugal. It opened on 15 June 2009 and is one of the Sea Life Centres in Europe, which are owned by Merlin Entertainments.","wpu":"Sea Life Porto","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Sea_Life.JPG/960px-Sea_Life.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Leça Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.201389,"lo":-8.712222,"d":2286,"ds":"The Leça Lighthouse (Portuguese: Farol de Leça), also known as the Farol de Boa Nova, is a lighthouse on the Atlantic coast located in Leça da Palmeira, in the municipality of Matosinhos in the Porto District of Portugal. It is the second-tallest lighthouse in Portugal.","wpu":"Leça Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Farol_de_Le%C3%A7a.jpg/960px-Farol_de_Le%C3%A7a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fort São João Baptista da Foz","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.148889,"lo":-8.674444,"d":4354,"ds":"The Fort São João Baptista da Foz (Forte de São João Baptista da Foz in Portuguese), is located in the parish of Foz do Douro, in the municipality and District of Porto, in Portugal. It stands in a dominant position at the mouth of the Douro river, overseeing the access the city of Porto via the river.","wpu":"Fort São João Baptista da Foz","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Aerial_photographs_of_Forte_de_S%C3%A3o_Jo%C3%A3o_Baptista_da_Foz_%282%29.jpg/960px-Aerial_photographs_of_Forte_de_S%C3%A3o_Jo%C3%A3o_Baptista_da_Foz_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fountain of Passeio Alegre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.148694,"lo":-8.672556,"d":4452,"ds":"The Fountain of Passeio Alegre (Portuguese: Chafariz do Passeio Alegre) is a fountain located in civil parish of Aldoar, Foz do Douro e Nevogilde, municipality of Porto in northern Portugal.","wpu":"Fountain of Passeio Alegre","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Chafariz_do_Passeio_Alegre.jpg/960px-Chafariz_do_Passeio_Alegre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Serralves","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.1585,"lo":-8.6577,"d":4467,"ds":"Serralves is a cultural institution located in Porto, Portugal. It includes a contemporary art museum, a park, and a villa, with each one of these being an example of contemporary architecture, Modernism, and Art Deco architecture. The museum, designed by Álvaro Siza Vieira, is now the second most visited museum in Portugal (almost 1 million visitors per year).","wpu":"Serralves","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Lonely_Dancer_%284937475766%29.jpg/960px-Lonely_Dancer_%284937475766%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lighthouse of São Miguel-o-Anjo","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.147111,"lo":-8.666722,"d":4866,"ds":"The Lighthouse of São Miguel-o-Anjo (Portuguese: Farol de São Miguel-o-Anjo) is a former hermitage and 16th century lighthouse, in the civil parish of Aldoar, Foz do Douro e Nevogilde, municipality of Porto, in the Portuguese Norte Region. The lighthouse of São Miguel-o-Anjo is Portugal's oldest existing lighthouse and one of the oldest in Europe.","wpu":"Lighthouse of São Miguel-o-Anjo","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Telegraph_Tower.jpg/960px-Telegraph_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Jardim Botânico do Porto","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.1536,"lo":-8.6426,"d":5811,"ds":"The Porto Botanical Garden (Portuguese: Jardim Botânico do Porto) is a botanical garden located in the gardens of the Campo Alegre Estate (Quinta do Campo Alegre) or Andresen House, in Porto, Portugal. Since 2015, it has been a part of the Museum of Natural History and Science of University of Porto (MHNC-UP).","wpu":"Jardim Botânico do Porto","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Jardim_Bot%C3%A2nico_Porto_-_tras.jpg/960px-Jardim_Bot%C3%A2nico_Porto_-_tras.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kadoorie Synagogue","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.155939,"lo":-8.636917,"d":6077,"ds":"The Kadoorie Mekor Haim Synagogue (Portuguese: Sinagoga Kadoorie Mekor Haim), also the Porto Synagogue (Portuguese: Sinagoga do Porto), is an Orthodox Jewish congregation and synagogue, located at 340 Guerra Junqueiro Street, in the civil parish of Lordelo do Ouro e Massarelos, the municipality of Porto, in the northern region of Portugal. Mekor haim is Hebrew for 'source of life'.","wpu":"Kadoorie Synagogue","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Kadoorie_Mekor_Haim_Synagogue.jpg/960px-Kadoorie_Mekor_Haim_Synagogue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Agramonte Cemetery","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.150556,"lo":-8.632333,"d":6715,"ds":"The Agramonte Cemetery is a cemetery in the city of Porto, in Portugal which dates back to 1855.","wpu":"Agramonte Cemetery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Jazigo_do_Conde_da_Trindade.jpg/960px-Jazigo_do_Conde_da_Trindade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Porto Tram Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.147706,"lo":-8.632836,"d":6856,"ds":"The Porto Tram Museum (Museu do Carro Eléctrico) is a museum operated by the Sociedade de Transportes Colectivos do Porto. It was inaugurated in 1992 and is installed in a former thermoelectric power station next to the River Douro in Massarelos, Porto, Portugal. It exhibits material related to the history of trams in Porto.","wpu":"Porto Tram Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Museu_Carro_Electrico.JPG/960px-Museu_Carro_Electrico.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church of São Martinho de Cedofeita","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.155792,"lo":-8.621697,"d":7218,"ds":"The Church of Cedofeita (Portuguese: Igreja de Cedofeita) is a medieval church in the civil parish of Cedofeita, municipality of Porto, in the northern Grande Porto Subregion of Portugal. The Church is a rare architectural example of a single-nave vaulted-ceiling temple, and the only one in the traditional Entre-Douro-e-Minho Province region of Portugal. It is classified as a National Monument.","wpu":"Church of São Martinho de Cedofeita","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Cedofeita-Igreja_Romanica_de_Cedofeita_%282%29.jpg/960px-Cedofeita-Igreja_Romanica_de_Cedofeita_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Almeida Garrett Library","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.148056,"lo":-8.626944,"d":7245,"ds":"Almeida Garrett Library (Portuguese: Biblioteca Almeida Garrett) is a library located in the civil parish of Lordelo do Ouro e Massarelos, in municipality of Porto, Portugal.","wpu":"Almeida Garrett Library","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Biblioteca_Almeida_Garrett_%28Porto%29.JPG/960px-Biblioteca_Almeida_Garrett_%28Porto%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tower of Pedro-Sem","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.149167,"lo":-8.625,"d":7319,"ds":"The Tower of Pedro-Sem (Portuguese: Torre do Palácio dos Terenas/Torre de Pedro-Sem/Torre da Marca) is a medieval fortification situated in the civil parish of Lordelo do Ouro e Massarelos, that protected the northern Portuguese city of Porto.","wpu":"Tower of Pedro-Sem","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Torre_Pedro-Sem_13.jpg/960px-Torre_Pedro-Sem_13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St James' Church, Porto","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":41.15001,"lo":-8.62403,"d":7341,"ds":"St James' Church is an English-speaking Anglican church in Porto (also known as Oporto), Portugal. It is part of the Diocese in Europe. The church is surrounded by a churchyard, and its history is closely tied with the British merchants of that city.","wpu":"St James' Church, Porto","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/66/British_Church_St_James_%28Porto%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Porto, also known in English as Oporto, is the second largest city in Portugal, after Lisbon. It is the capital of the Porto District and one of the Iberian Peninsula's major urban areas. Porto city proper, which is the entire municipality of Porto, is small compared to its metropolitan area, with an estimated population of 273,476 people in a municipal area of 41.42 km2 (16 sq mi).","wpu":"Porto","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG/960px-Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}